{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)"},{"text":" gives each destination its batches in the order the events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"text":" returns. Batches that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops its oldest batch when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full, so a destination that falls behind loses batches rather than holding up the others.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" should return promptly and honour cancellation: a delivery waits for it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is cancelled. A destination handles its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is what tells the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" is set may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have reached it in an earlier run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/destination"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Destination.swift#L23","fileName":"Destination.swift"},"symbolKind":"protocol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","externalID":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","navigatorTitle